  "asked": "Headless build in Brett's AmberX-AXF repo (worktree, branch claude/approval-expand). Read CLAUDE.md + _claude/shared/rules/RULES.md. Opus, one session. Git auth is in your environment (GIT_CONFIG_*); just git push. 0. Wait (poll every 30 s, max 60 min) until origin/main contains the approval-source build (git log origin/main --oneline | grep -i 'approval-source\\|who asked\\|X-Axhub-Session'). Then git merge origin/main. Brett: make every approval row EXPANDABLE. Caret (chevron) on the FAR RIGHT of the row. Tap row or caret -> it drops open in place (no navigation) with real details: - full reason title + description (Claude's words) - exact command / arguments (monospace, scrollable, copy button; secrets hidden as the server already does) - who asked: source badge, session/build/agent name, client - tool + policy (veto/confirm) + risk tags - timeline: requested, countdown/decided time, decided by, ran at, duration - result once run: exit code + last lines of output, link to the full approval page - Approve (green) + Deny (red) inside too while waiting Apply to: axhub-web approvals list, the Waiting for approvals dropdown, AmberX hub view, console approvals banner (shared component, do it once). Expanded state survives live refreshes (no collapse, no flicker, update in place). Framework controls + theme/scale tokens only. Tests (expand/collapse, stays open on refresh, buttons inside work). Full local test block from .github/workflows/android.yml + theme/controls/lifecycle checks green. Commit, git fetch && git merge origin/main, retest, git push origin HEAD:main (retry until it lands). Short report at _claude/builds/reports/approval-expand.md.",
